  "path_normalization": "Embedded command and diagnostic paths are repository-relative. report_sha256 fields identify the original, unnormalized reports.",
  "overall_arm64e_complete": false,
  "scope": "Controlled PAC execution for complete recovered NativeAnalysis fixed C prototypes with scalar, 128-bit integer and direct record/HFA values. ABI recovery accuracy itself is not established by supplied IR fixtures. All five unchanged Mach-O routes require original exception classes. Raw indirect calls are controls. Indirect by-value copies, hidden results, signed exception unwinding, authenticated whole-image execution, native Apple PAC and exact fault PC/full ESR remain unqualified.",
  "base_revision": "a72fcd510e017ea95aeedb26f84a86ed3cde894c",
  "model_producer_revision": "3e2f9b76773f09dbefb3e6e92ceed74f815cbd90",
  "additional_test_revision": "2e533756afd61175a96365535c0786ce27ef607c",
  "environment_repository": "https://github.com/gmh5225/test_mac_intel",
  "environment_revision": "71462f4faeeafefd28d5dd43ba8e52e904334b21",
  "environment_pr": "https://github.com/gmh5225/test_mac_intel/pull/3",
  "changes": [
    "Reuse the validated physical machine-call bridge for complete recovered fixed Darwin C prototypes, preserving original authenticated target, key, modifier and result pieces through LLVM and both C routes.",
    "Use declared caller parameter types while marshalling floating values; reject authenticated native single-Q 128-bit SIMD carriers, indirect by-value copies and hidden results until their separate transport is proved.",
    "Admit multi-start pages in the strict whole-image dependency reader while preserving signing, slot, CPU ABI and import identity. Reject malformed overflow lists and duplicate or partially overlapping chain storage across bind/rebase phases.",
    "Check Swift aggregate logical return values after scalar byte projection, and separately keep full-register consumers dependent on the actual call clobber. This adjusts a stale IR-shape test without changing production Swift semantics."
  ],
